  unchanged file                                   -> accepted
  truncated to 40 bytes                            -> file shorter than an ELF64 header
  truncated to 200 bytes                           -> program header table outside the file
  first byte changed (bad magic)                   -> bad ELF magic
  class byte says 32-bit                           -> not a 64-bit little-endian ELF file
  program header offset huge                       -> program header table outside the file
  second segment moved onto the first (overlap)    -> segments overlap
  entry point outside every segment                -> entry point not inside an executable segment
  first segment's file offset at end of file       -> segment data outside the file
random damage: 200000 damaged copies, 123791 rejected, 76209 still accepted, no crash
